## Bottom line

The highest-value business story is:

"When a DDoS or severe overload event hits multiple services, brownout-policy-compiler gives the incident commander, network lead, security lead, service owners, and GRC lead a deterministic, business-aware, rollback-safe set of temporary brownout candidates so critical workflows stay available while lower-priority services are intentionally degraded under review."

That story is realistic, credible, and high ROI because it aligns with current DDoS trends, NIST incident-response guidance, CISA mission-impact guidance, SRE overload patterns, and outage-cost data.
